course: dictionary
lesson: 4482
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A harvester is someone or something that gathers crops, such as wheat or seeds. The word has more than one meaning, so the words around it show you which one the writer means. «A combine harvester cuts the wheat, beats out the grains and blows away the straw at once.» Cutting, beating and blowing are jobs for a machine, so here a harvester is a machine.
explain: «...where weary harvesters could line up in scores along the table.» Weary means tired, and people line up, not machines. So here harvesters are people who gather crops. Always ask: what could this thing do or feel? Then choose the meaning that fits.
fact: A harvester can be a machine, a person or an animal.
fact: A combine harvester cuts wheat, beats out the grains and blows the straw away in one go.
fact: A harvester ant is an animal that collects seeds for food.
fact: The word harvester can also name a daddy-long-legs-like creature, which is called a harvestman.
fact: In maths problems, a harvester may cut a field in a certain number of hours, so you may be working out a rate.
exercise: «A combine harvester cuts the wheat, beats out the grains and blows the straw away.» In this sentence, a harvester is | An animal that collects seeds | A person who gathers crops | A grain plant | *A machine
exercise: «...where weary harvesters could line up in scores along the table.» Here, harvesters are | Ants that collect seeds | *People who gather crops | A daddy-long-legs-like creature | A machine that cuts wheat
exercise: Which harvester collects seeds for food? | A machine that blows away straw | A farmer who sows grain | *A harvester ant | A combine harvester
test: «In summer a combine harvester cuts the stalks in one go.» What is a combine harvester? | A type of straw | A person who gathers crops | *A machine that gathers crops | An animal that collects food
test: Which meaning fits a harvester that collects seeds for food? | A machine that cuts wheat | A person who sows grain | A tall grain plant | *An animal, such as a harvester ant
exam: Jayden says a harvester is always a machine. Is he right? | *No, it can be a machine, a person or an animal, so check the context | Yes, but only in maths problems | Yes, it is always a machine | No, it can be a machine, a person or an animal
